llama-mmid-helper-par.patch (was llama-moe-expert-table.patch), 2026-11-11 - helper-only record
Base: llama.cpp master 7592b61d3 (ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmid.cu only). Apply: git apply llama-mmid-helper-par.patch

What it does
  At this base, MUL_MAT_ID's MMQ path already reads experts in place (x + expert*stride_channel_x) and quantizes
  activations once per token and scatters them (quantize_scatter_mmq_q8_1). So an expert pointer table
  (moe_mmq_tab.cuh) has nothing to remove when all experts are resident. The avoidable MoE layout work left is
  mm_ids_helper: one warp per expert scans all n_tokens serially, about 97 us per call at ub 2048.
  This patch adds mm_ids_helper_par: 32 warps per expert, each owning a contiguous token chunk. Pass 1 counts, a
  block-level scan gives each warp's base, and pass 2 writes ids_dst/ids_src1 directly, with no n_tokens shared
  buffer. Order is preserved, so ids_src1, ids_dst and tile_spec are identical, and the MMQ results are bitwise
  identical. It is used for templated n_expert_used, warp size 32, and n_tokens >= GGML_CUDA_MMID_PAR_MIN
  (default 256; 0 = always). Decode and small batches keep the original kernel.

Measured (RTX 5090, a MoE GGUF (IQ1_M), all-VRAM -ngl 99, -t 8 -b 4096 -ub 2048, cold unique-nonce
prompts, engine prompt tok/s, 3 reps x 2 alternating passes, n=6)
  10k (9,836 tok): stock 5,948 [5,913-5,988]  patched 6,163 [6,139-6,192]  +3.6%
   2.7k          : stock 4,332 [4,208-4,372]  patched 4,395 [4,211-4,531]  (within noise)
  patched -ub 6144 (-b 8192): 10k 5,841 [5,348-5,882], 2.7k 5,064 [5,019-5,120]
  nsys 10k ub2048: mm_ids_helper 82.1 ms (846 calls) -> mm_ids_helper_par 26.2 ms (705 calls) + 0.4 ms of
  small-batch mm_ids_helper. Kernel-busy time drops from 1,416 to 1,363 ms; every other family is unchanged.
Correctness: test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT_ID with GGML_CUDA_MMID_PAR_MIN=0: 967/967 pass. Greedy --temp 0, four prompts
  (397-6,311 tokens, 96 generated tokens each): text and top-5 logprobs bitwise identical to stock.
Evidence: boltbeam-runs/llama-expert-table-20261111.md and boltbeam-runs/llama-expert-table-20261111/

